From 9c27ca9a0657338852c7d3e59561d424fc036fde Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: halt95 <halt95@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 07:58:38 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 58/58] executor: detect a fail-closed fault or death on any
 rank

A fault on a non-zero TP rank could hang the engine: the worker's sentinel pipe
was inherited by a helper process and stayed open, so the monitor never saw
the exit. Earlier releases carry the same monitor and fail-closed exit path.

- Worker exit is detected by pidfd, with the sentinel as fallback, before and
  after READY and for every worker through the whole initialisation window.
- A per-worker fault pipe: ple_fail_closed writes one byte before os._exit and
  the monitor starts the failure ladder at once; the fd stays registered
  through worker teardown.
- worker_main marks inherited pipes close-on-exec.
- Any unexpected busy-loop failure exits 1; the termination ladder uses
  time.monotonic(); forced-exit paths no longer wait on logging.
- Tests on real fork/spawn workers for rank 0 and rank 1, with and without an
  fd-inheriting helper.
